WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.309
An agent can remember thousands of

2
00:00:02.309 --> 00:00:04.061
facts and still fail at the

3
00:00:04.061 --> 00:00:06.370
moment that matters. The problem is

4
00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:08.520
not storage alone. It is deciding

5
00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:10.511
what should be active, what can

6
00:00:10.511 --> 00:00:13.139
be discovered, what evidence supports a

7
00:00:13.139 --> 00:00:15.209
conclusion, and what a caller is

8
00:00:15.209 --> 00:00:17.757
allowed to see. MDBrain addresses that

9
00:00:17.757 --> 00:00:20.305
full path. It combines long-term memory

10
00:00:20.305 --> 00:00:22.535
from Memongo with a governed wiki,

11
00:00:22.535 --> 00:00:25.322
then delivers typed context through HTTP,

12
00:00:25.322 --> 00:00:27.870
MCP, and agent framework integrations.

13
00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:29.781
The repository is a Bun and

14
00:00:29.781 --> 00:00:32.822
Turborepo monorepo with four deployable

15
00:00:32.822 --> 00:00:34.647
surfaces. A Hono API is the

16
00:00:34.647 --> 00:00:37.340
central runtime. A standard-input MCP

17
00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:39.946
server exposes the same contract as

18
00:00:39.946 --> 00:00:42.900
tools. A Next.js application provides the

19
00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:45.420
product site, demos, and an operator

20
00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:47.766
console. Mintlify publishes the

21
00:00:47.766 --> 00:00:50.980
documentation. Shared packages sit beneath

22
00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:54.021
those applications, so protocol adapters

23
00:00:54.021 --> 00:00:56.801
remain thin and domain behavior stays

24
00:00:56.801 --> 00:00:57.670
in one place.

25
00:00:57.670 --> 00:01:00.554
Every supported operation crosses the API

26
00:01:00.554 --> 00:01:03.519
boundary. The application composes content

27
00:01:03.519 --> 00:01:05.602
checks, CORS, rate limits, bearer

28
00:01:05.602 --> 00:01:08.486
authentication, and scoped authorization

29
00:01:08.486 --> 00:01:11.130
before the version-one router handles a

30
00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:13.453
request. From there, memory calls go

31
00:01:13.453 --> 00:01:15.456
to the Memongo bridge and wiki

32
00:01:15.456 --> 00:01:17.219
calls go to the wiki engine.

33
00:01:17.219 --> 00:01:19.542
Health and readiness are separate.

34
00:01:19.542 --> 00:01:22.587
Readiness verifies dependencies, including

35
00:01:22.587 --> 00:01:25.151
the remote memory contract, before the

36
00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:27.394
service claims that it can accept

37
00:01:27.394 --> 00:01:27.955
traffic.

38
00:01:27.955 --> 00:01:30.071
MDBrain does not embed a second

39
00:01:30.071 --> 00:01:32.919
memory database engine. The memory bridge

40
00:01:32.919 --> 00:01:35.767
calls a separate Memongo service through

41
00:01:35.767 --> 00:01:38.045
a captured version two point zero

42
00:01:38.045 --> 00:01:40.812
point one contract. Before traffic flows,

43
00:01:40.812 --> 00:01:43.660
the client checks the advertised version

44
00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:46.182
and OpenAPI digest. Operation policy

45
00:01:46.182 --> 00:01:48.949
selects the method, path, credential type,

46
00:01:48.949 --> 00:01:51.797
deadline, retry behavior, and idempotency

47
00:01:51.797 --> 00:01:54.726
requirement. This boundary keeps upgrades

48
00:01:54.726 --> 00:01:57.493
explicit and prevents a remote contract

49
00:01:57.493 --> 00:02:00.097
change from silently altering memory

50
00:02:00.097 --> 00:02:00.748
behavior.

51
00:02:00.748 --> 00:02:02.970
The repository owns a separate

52
00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:05.363
MongoDB-backed wiki. A page is more

53
00:02:05.363 --> 00:02:07.756
than prose. It has claims, evidence,

54
00:02:07.756 --> 00:02:09.978
open questions, relationships,

55
00:02:09.978 --> 00:02:12.883
permissions, lifecycle state, backlinks,

56
00:02:12.883 --> 00:02:15.704
and revision history. Writes normalize

57
00:02:15.704 --> 00:02:18.524
content, resolve transclusion targets,

58
00:02:18.524 --> 00:02:21.515
update backlinks, detect contradictions,

59
00:02:21.515 --> 00:02:23.993
reject near duplicates, and record

60
00:02:23.993 --> 00:02:26.899
snapshots. Reads apply governance after

61
00:02:26.899 --> 00:02:29.719
retrieval. That order matters because a

62
00:02:29.719 --> 00:02:32.368
relevant page is still unusable when

63
00:02:32.368 --> 00:02:34.419
the caller lacks scope or the

64
00:02:34.419 --> 00:02:36.727
page has moved into a restricted

65
00:02:36.727 --> 00:02:37.154
state.

66
00:02:37.154 --> 00:02:39.577
Wiki search can combine Atlas vector

67
00:02:39.577 --> 00:02:41.374
search with lexical search,

68
00:02:41.374 --> 00:02:44.032
reciprocal-rank fusion, optional Voyage

69
00:02:44.032 --> 00:02:46.611
reranking, and graph expansion. Recipes

70
00:02:46.611 --> 00:02:48.955
trade latency for depth. Capability

71
00:02:48.955 --> 00:02:51.378
detection keeps the system honest: if

72
00:02:51.378 --> 00:02:53.879
a deployment lacks one advanced stage,

73
00:02:53.879 --> 00:02:56.224
search degrades to a supported path

74
00:02:56.224 --> 00:02:58.725
instead of pretending the feature ran.

75
00:02:58.725 --> 00:03:01.382
Governance remains the final filter, and

76
00:03:01.382 --> 00:03:04.117
the result records enough provenance for

77
00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:06.696
callers to understand which retrieval

78
00:03:06.696 --> 00:03:08.025
stages contributed.

79
00:03:08.025 --> 00:03:10.458
Memory delivery separates what should

80
00:03:10.458 --> 00:03:12.302
enter the prompt now from what

81
00:03:12.302 --> 00:03:14.735
should remain discoverable. The active

82
00:03:14.735 --> 00:03:17.168
slate is small and immediate. Discovery

83
00:03:17.168 --> 00:03:19.527
projections preserve candidates for

84
00:03:19.527 --> 00:03:21.666
follow-up. Context bundles combine

85
00:03:21.666 --> 00:03:24.099
selected memory with wiki material and

86
00:03:24.099 --> 00:03:26.163
trust metadata. This lets an agent

87
00:03:26.163 --> 00:03:28.154
spend tokens on the present task

88
00:03:28.154 --> 00:03:30.661
without losing access to deeper history.

89
00:03:30.661 --> 00:03:33.021
The client returns typed receipts and

90
00:03:33.021 --> 00:03:35.527
source information, so applications can

91
00:03:35.527 --> 00:03:37.739
trace what was delivered instead of

92
00:03:37.739 --> 00:03:39.804
accepting an opaque block of text.

93
00:03:39.803 --> 00:03:41.892
A memory write can also request

94
00:03:41.892 --> 00:03:44.544
wiki promotion. MDBrain handles that as

95
00:03:44.544 --> 00:03:46.954
durable delivery, not as one fragile

96
00:03:46.954 --> 00:03:49.284
request chain. An intent moves from

97
00:03:49.284 --> 00:03:52.016
pending to dispatching, then records the

98
00:03:52.016 --> 00:03:54.748
Memongo receipt. Transient or ambiguous

99
00:03:54.748 --> 00:03:57.158
failures become retryable with the

100
00:03:57.158 --> 00:04:00.131
original idempotency key. Promotion starts

101
00:04:00.131 --> 00:04:02.702
only after memory delivery succeeds. A

102
00:04:02.702 --> 00:04:05.514
bounded reconciler leases eligible work,

103
00:04:05.514 --> 00:04:07.844
retries safely, and can dead-letter

104
00:04:07.844 --> 00:04:10.737
exhausted intents. The state machine makes

105
00:04:10.737 --> 00:04:13.549
partial failure visible and recoverable.

106
00:04:13.549 --> 00:04:15.995
Consumers do not need to understand

107
00:04:15.995 --> 00:04:17.707
the server internals. The

108
00:04:17.707 --> 00:04:20.724
zero-runtime-dependency TypeScript client

109
00:04:20.724 --> 00:04:23.170
models the public HTTP contract. The

110
00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:25.615
MCP application maps that client to

111
00:04:25.615 --> 00:04:28.061
thirty tools. The tools package adds

112
00:04:28.061 --> 00:04:30.263
AI SDK functions plus Vercel and

113
00:04:30.263 --> 00:04:32.872
OpenAI-compatible middleware. The web

114
00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:35.073
console uses the client from the

115
00:04:35.073 --> 00:04:38.008
browser for live operations. Because these

116
00:04:38.008 --> 00:04:40.046
paths converge on the same API,

117
00:04:40.046 --> 00:04:42.655
contract changes can be reviewed once

118
00:04:42.655 --> 00:04:45.101
and then propagated to each adapter.

119
00:04:45.101 --> 00:04:47.393
The security model is layered. Bearer

120
00:04:47.393 --> 00:04:49.907
credentials resolve to principals with

121
00:04:49.907 --> 00:04:52.347
scopes and capabilities. Tenant memory

122
00:04:52.347 --> 00:04:54.344
credentials stay separate from

123
00:04:54.344 --> 00:04:56.784
control-plane credentials. Server-side

124
00:04:56.784 --> 00:04:59.520
request forgery checks constrain outbound

125
00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:02.182
destinations. Redaction keeps secrets out

126
00:05:02.182 --> 00:05:04.770
of logs and errors. Transaction-dependent

127
00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:06.988
wiki mutations fail closed when the

128
00:05:06.988 --> 00:05:09.354
database cannot provide the required

129
00:05:09.354 --> 00:05:12.016
guarantees. Rate limits and content checks

130
00:05:12.016 --> 00:05:14.531
guard the public edge, while idempotency

131
00:05:14.531 --> 00:05:16.897
protects writes that may have crossed

132
00:05:16.897 --> 00:05:19.115
a network boundary before a timeout.

133
00:05:19.115 --> 00:05:21.630
At the measured main-branch snapshot,

134
00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:24.226
MDBrain contained ten workspaces, one

135
00:05:24.226 --> 00:05:27.065
hundred and one implementation files, and

136
00:05:27.065 --> 00:05:29.417
forty-eight test files. TypeScript

137
00:05:29.417 --> 00:05:32.013
dominated the tracked text corpus. The

138
00:05:32.013 --> 00:05:34.204
largest active sources were the

139
00:05:34.204 --> 00:05:36.962
version-one router, the generated-by-hand

140
00:05:36.962 --> 00:05:39.801
OpenAPI specification, and the MCP server.

141
00:05:39.801 --> 00:05:42.884
Those concentrations are useful navigation

142
00:05:42.884 --> 00:05:45.642
landmarks, but they are also refactoring

143
00:05:45.642 --> 00:05:48.075
pressure points. The wiki engine has

144
00:05:48.075 --> 00:05:50.915
the broadest package export surface, with

145
00:05:50.915 --> 00:05:53.267
one hundred and forty-two exported

146
00:05:53.267 --> 00:05:53.835
symbols.

147
00:05:53.835 --> 00:05:56.497
The shortest path through MDBrain is

148
00:05:56.497 --> 00:05:58.471
to start at the boundary you

149
00:05:58.471 --> 00:06:00.789
need to change. For HTTP behavior,

150
00:06:00.789 --> 00:06:02.678
begin in the API router and

151
00:06:02.678 --> 00:06:05.340
specification. For memory semantics,

152
00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:08.087
follow the bridge policy and captured

153
00:06:08.087 --> 00:06:11.092
Memongo contract. For governed knowledge,

154
00:06:11.092 --> 00:06:13.410
begin at the wiki engine exports

155
00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:15.814
and store. For agent access, follow

156
00:06:15.814 --> 00:06:17.789
the client into MCP or tools.

157
00:06:17.789 --> 00:06:20.193
Then run the focused Vitest suite,

158
00:06:20.193 --> 00:06:22.769
type checks, and Biome checks before

159
00:06:22.769 --> 00:06:25.001
the full Turbo pipeline. The key

160
00:06:25.001 --> 00:06:27.319
idea is simple: memory, knowledge,

161
00:06:27.319 --> 00:06:30.238
delivery, and authority remain separate,

162
00:06:30.238 --> 00:06:32.900
but compose through typed contracts.
